WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.767
-It is so great to see you.

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.467
-Thanks. You too.
-They love you.

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:05.868
We love you.
-Thanks. Thanks.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:08.300
-We were talking backstage about
your little baby, your son.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.601
One and a half.
[ Audience awws ]

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:12.133
[ Applause ]
What a doll.

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:14.000
-I love him so much.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.801
-How is fatherhood?
How is parenthood?

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:19.567
-Do you want TV version
or real life?

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.734
-I don't want the Internet
talking but tell me real life.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.934
Tell me both.
-Here's the honest truth.

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:26.267
I love my son, gosh,
more than life itself.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.701
He's the best thing
in the world.

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:31.501
And I never really understood
love until my baby was born.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:34.033
[ Audience awws ]
However, to balance it out,

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:38.467
no one warns you that you really
are just going to become nuts.

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:41.167
It's so hard. It's so hard.

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:44.400
I love him so much but I'm so
excited for bedtime every day.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.701
But then as soon as I put him
into bed, I watch the monitor

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.300
thinking, "I miss him so much."

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.567
I miss him so much.
-You have the monitor?

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:52.901
-Yeah.
-You're at that phase.

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:54.434
-Yeah. I love him.

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:56.033
I just need him to sleep
every now and then.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:57.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.067
-It's a lot of work.
-I need a break.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:02.334
I'm almost 40. I can't --
[ Woman gasps ]

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:03.601
Wow, I love the gasp.

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:07.567
-How is the baby's style?

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.934
-He's a baby!

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.334
-I know. I'm sorry. I know.

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:12.467
But you, I'm assuming --

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:14.634
-Okay. You've got two, right?
-Yes.

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:16.234
-You know this all too well.

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:18.868
When they're a toddler,
they're vomiting all the time.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:21.234
They're pooping all the time.
There's blowouts.

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:24.100
Like, they're muddy.
-Blowouts.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.234
[ Laughter ]
-There are constant blowouts.

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:29.968
And so I don't put him
in a nice outfit.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:33.968
Like people, very kind people,
entertainers will send, like,

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.367
designer things
as a "Oh, my gosh,

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:37.033
I can't believe you're a parent.
Here you are.

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:38.167
Here's something fancy
for your child."

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:39.267
-No, I can't believe that. I go,

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:41.167
"You've clearly never had a
child."

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.167
-Yeah, I'm never putting him in
that.

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:44.300
Thank you for wasting
your money.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.434
That's never going on my child.

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:47.501
-No, ever.
The baby just spits up.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:49.300
-He's in cheapo onesies.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.734
-Onesies, that's all you need.
-That's it.

00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:53.200
And also I get a size too small

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.400
so he looks
really fat and sausaged.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.434
[ Laughter ]
Aww! Aww!

00:01:57.434 --> 00:01:58.767
-Nothing better than that.
-It's so cute.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:01.534
I mean, he can't move,
but I, like, don't care.

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:03.601
"You look great.
You look great, kid."

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:05.300
-That's so funny.
-Yeah, so nice.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.133
-You and your husband just
celebrated 15 years?

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.534
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:12.667
Thank you very much.
Thank you very much.

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.033
Dream. Love it.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.767
-Isn't that wild? 15 years.

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.634
-It flew by. I can't believe
it's been 15 years.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:18.934
I still feel 17.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:21.834
I can't believe I've been with
him since I was 2. Yeah.

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:23.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.868
-When you walk around --
When Tan France walks around

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:28.100
New York City, do people just
freak out and go like,

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:29.734
"Love you, dude"?

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:31.634
-It's so nice. Okay.
Here's the thing.

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:34.601
You're all so nice in New York.
It's lovely.

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.667
So, I live in Salt Lake City,
Utah. Hi.

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:39.100
I live in Salt Lake City, Utah,
and it's different.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:42.167
When I'm in other places, people
will just give you a hug,

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:45.100
and they want to say hello, and
they're really sweet about it.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.934
When I'm in New York, you guys
do something really weird here.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:51.601
You're too cool for school,
which is sometimes very nice.

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:54.701
And so, they'll kind of --
There's this thing where they'll

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:57.701
kind of look over, and they'll
smile, and they'll move

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.434
their hair as they're walking
towards you.

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:02.334
So it's kind of like they're
flirting with you.

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:06.667
I'm like, "Are you DTF or do you
know me from TV?"

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:07.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:10.200
Legit today, there was
this woman walking --

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.934
older lady, senior lady
walking towards me.

00:03:12.934 --> 00:03:14.701
And I'm like, "Grandma wants to
[bleep]."

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:16.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:18.567
And then, my husband
reminded me --

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:20.200
I know you're not allowed to
swear. I'm sorry.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.767
-No, we'll cut that out.
We'll cut that right out, yeah.

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:23.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:25.801
-But then, yeah, my husband
reminded me,

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:27.400
no, she's not flirting with you.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.934
She probably just knows you
from TV.

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:30.834
-Yeah, of course.
Everyone loves you, though.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.434
-But they don't say hi.

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.200
They just do the flirty thing.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.634
I'm like, "Just talk to me,
man."

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:38.601
-It's New York. Yeah, you got to
be cool, man.

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:42.200
"Next in Fashion." It's a
fantastic show on Netflix.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.801
It comes out tomorrow.
Gigi Hadid is your cohost.

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:46.167
And she's one of my faves.

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:48.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
-She's the best.

00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:50.601
-She's A-plus.
She's A-plus-plus.

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:52.300
-I love her.
-And I love how comfortable

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.334
you guys are with each other
and just riff off each other.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:58.033
And she's so funny. And she gets
to be funny on this show.

00:03:58.033 --> 00:04:01.000
And she was telling me she met
you because she was depressed

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.601
and she just loves "Queer Eye"
so much.

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:05.400
And she ended up FaceTiming you

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.067
and invited you
over to her house.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:09.434
And you came over to her house.
-Yeah. It was lovely.

00:04:09.434 --> 00:04:12.100
So, not necessarily depressed.
She was just having a bad day.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.467
[ Laughter ]
-I'm sorry. I'm embellishing.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:16.000
I'm embellishing.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.067
-She was having a rough few
days, and she'd been --

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:21.200
-Wait. You said a bad day.
Now it's getting worse.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.601
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:27.934
She had a shocking five years.
And there I was, savior --

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.567
-On a horse.
-Yes.

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:31.934
That's what this lady needs,
a knight in shining armor.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.701
And so, no, "Queer Eye"
just been out

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:35.801
for like maybe three weeks,
four weeks.

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:37.968
And she had been binge-watching
"Queer Eye."

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:40.634
And she felt like she was
my best friend

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.634
and I was her best friend.
-Immediately.

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:44.801
-Yeah, as many people do when
they watch the show.

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:46.767
-But did you freak out?
'Cause that's Gigi Hadid.

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:48.501
-Yeah. So, it was Antoni's
birthday,

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:50.667
and she wanted to FaceTime
through a friend.

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:52.467
And so, I was like,
"Yeah, let's FaceTime."

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.167
And she said, "Do you want to
come over?"

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:56.234
And it was Antoni's -- Antoni's
my castmate on "Queer Eye."

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:58.167
And I turn to Antoni and I was
like, "Hey, I know I was meant

00:04:58.167 --> 00:04:59.534
to take you out
for a birthday lunch.

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:01.868
But can we go to Gigi's house
instead?"

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.234
And he was like,
"Mm-hmm, let's do that. Yep."

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:04.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:07.367
'Cause she was the first famous
person we were hanging out with.

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:09.367
And we went over to her house
and it was just --

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:12.834
I was in shock the whole time
thinking, "That's Gigi Hadid."

00:05:12.834 --> 00:05:16.167
-Yes. I mean, unbelievable, on
the cover of "Vogue" magazine.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:18.868
-Yeah, talking to me
like I'm a normal person.

00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:20.667
Like, that's insane.
-You are!

00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:22.334
Yeah, I love her.

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:24.934
What can we set up for this clip
to let everyone know

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:26.667
what "Next in Fashion" --

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:29.067
-"Next in Fashion"
is a wonderful show.

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:31.033
We're on season two.
Gigi and I host it together.

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:32.200
We had the time of our lives.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.300
We are looking for
incredible designers.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.734
We have 12 incredible designers
who, in my opinion, are

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:39.801
so impressive and you're going
to fall in love with them.

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:41.434
They have the best
personalities.

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:44.334
And the fashion is major.

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:45.767
-Yeah.
-Major.

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:47.467
-Yeah, okay. Good.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:49.534
Here's Tan France
in "Next in Fashion."

00:05:49.534 --> 00:05:50.667
Take a look.

00:05:50.667 --> 00:05:53.634
-I mean, her Instagram name is
slimfix71.

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:59.300
-Oh, my God, I love that that's
your mum's Insta.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.167
Should we call Mom?
FaceTime Mom?

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:03.968
-Oh, my God.

00:06:03.968 --> 00:06:05.901
-Hi, Slim.
-Hi, Mama.

00:06:05.901 --> 00:06:08.534
-How're you doing?
-Oh, we're so well.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:11.100
Why did you not let her dress
herself as a kid?

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.234
-She wanted to actually dress
less.

00:06:14.234 --> 00:06:17.234
-[ Laughs ]
-Oh!

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:18.501
-Oh, Amari.

00:06:18.501 --> 00:06:20.567
-Do you love what she wears now?

00:06:20.567 --> 00:06:23.067
-Ehh.
-Oh!

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:24.200
-Wow!

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.434
-My mom is out here just telling
all my business.

00:06:27.434 --> 00:06:30.467
-Only moms.
Only moms can do that.

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:33.968
-You are going to love
these people.

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:35.133
They're amazing.

00:06:35.133 --> 00:06:36.801
I do want to say one thing
about it, though.

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:38.667
Don't expect to see
a little black dress.

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:40.300
We're not about it. Don't.
Not interested.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.100
-Too simple.
-Yeah, we're not looking for

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:45.267
something you can buy today
anywhere in any store.

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:46.868
We're looking to be inspired by

00:06:46.868 --> 00:06:49.334
something new,
fresh, interesting.

00:06:49.334 --> 00:06:51.100
Even if you hate it,
that's fine.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:52.400
We just want you to think
about it.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.667
-Let's think about it and be
the "Next in Fashion."

00:06:54.667 --> 00:06:57.868
I get it. It begins streaming
tomorrow on Netflix.

00:06:57.868 --> 00:06:59.968
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

00:06:59.968 --> 00:07:01.467
Tan France, once again.

